ey passed this license plate  now this plate is from carb account II a  reference to carburetor County the  fictional county in cars where Radiator  Springs is located also the registered  city on the plate is torque ville  another fictional setting in the Cars  universe they rescue four key from Gabby  Gabby and Beau slides in uses her staff  to sweep the leg while doing so she  passes a commemorative plate with this  sword logo this is the crest of Merida's  family clan from brave woody allowed  Gabby to take his voice box but Gabby's  intended plan to use her voice to win  over the girl harmony fails because  harmony sucks and she tosses Gabby aside  but thanks to four key and bow what he  realizes that this can be his purpose  helping toys like Gabby who feel lost to  find their new forever kids because he  learned from his battle with lot so that  not all toys have to end up that way and  in doing so this Pixar film is able to  return back to the older Pixar rules a  story with no villain because not all  stories need a source of evil that needs  to be conquered sometimes the battle  could just be an inner one with a  character learning the key lesson  meanwhile buzzes gag in this movie is  taking literally the pre-recorded voices  inside him at one point he taps it over  and over and one of the voices says open  the pod bay doors which is of course a  nod to the famous line in Kubrick's 2001  a Space Odyssey open the pod bay doors  help in Dukes buzz parallel continues  with his big jump at the end which he  does with his eyes closed just like how  buzz closed his eyes while attempting to  fly in the first film  Duke passes over the hole  moon and out of the famous shot in ET  and woody says goodbye to his old  friends he passes on his sheriff's badge  to Jesse and like having his pull-string  removed this is the final visual  connecting him to Andy into Bonnie  he's severing his tether to the kids who  no longer need him and we learned that  woody Beau and the rest are headed to a  town called New Stanton which is a nod  to Andrew Stanton the longtime Pixar  animator and writer director who  directed films like Finding Nemo in  wall-e and the film's final exchange  buzz leaves on the RV waving to his  longtime buddy saying to infinity and  woody watches them go completing the  phrase with and beyond this movie  reestablishes this famous line from a  meaningless commercialized toy  catchphrase - the perfect description of  Woody's destiny infinity is by  definition undefined it just goes on and  on and on just like these toys do and  now with a new purpose that could get  redefined again and again as Woody's  future takes them on a new path it is  now Woody's turn to go to infinity and  beyond  now I broke down this movie's  post-credit scenes in another video go  check that out but my question for you  is which movie do you think had the  better ending Toy Story 3 or Toy Story 4  comment down below with your thoughts  and follow me on instagram and twitter  at EA boss and subscribe to new rock  stars for in-depth breakdowns of all the  movies that you love and now that this  breakdown is over let's play things out  with some Randy Newman UK the freedom  you gave me  [Music]
 

